// Calibration: Block on Severe Incompleteness
// Purpose: Hard safety gate when data is critically incomplete
// Category: Data Quality → Safety Gate (Hard Block)
// Use Case: mcp-trace-gate scenarios, required field validation
//
// WHAT IS COMPLETENESS?
// Fraction of requested fields that were actually returned.
// Calculation: (present_fields AND requested_fields) / requested_fields
//
// Examples:
//   - Requested 10 fields, got 8 → completeness = 0.8 (✅ allow)
//   - Requested 10 fields, got 4 → completeness = 0.4 (🔶 threshold)
//   - Requested 10 fields, got 2 → completeness = 0.2 (❌ block)
//
// THRESHOLD: 0.4 (40%)
// If less than 40% of required data present, that's a hard block.
// Agent lacks critical context; execution continues at serious risk.
//
// VERDICT: BLOCK execution, escalate to review
// Data too incomplete to safely proceed.

completeness < 0.4
